A quick fix if this setting is needed is to scope the setting in `schema/elasticsearch/visibility/cluster_settings_v7.json` to only turn off `auto_create_index` for temporal visibility index, but leave it on otherwise (that might also mess with existing patterns since it is a dynamic setting it could override previously defined disallow rules). 

```
{
  "persistent": {
    "action.auto_create_index": "-temporal_visibility_v1*,+*"
  }
}
```

This would follow the index pattern of the template, `"index_patterns": ["temporal_visibility_v1*"]` in `schema/elasticsearch/visibility/versioned/v14/index_template_v7.json`

But it would be preferable not to rely on this setting.

[Elasticsearch Automatically create data streams and indices documentation](https://www.elastic.co/docs/api/doc/elasticsearch/operation/operation-create)
